# Pair — Lead + Reviewer
#
# A Lead does the work directly and a Reviewer checks it before anything
# ships -- the smallest team that gets a second, independent opinion.
# Reviewer runs on a different provider/model than Lead when you have more
# than one configured, so it isn't reviewing itself.
#
# This file uses ${Provider1..2}/${Model1..2} placeholders instead of naming
# a specific provider -- `lmctl quickrun` fills them in with YOUR configured
# providers/models (recorded by `lmctl init`), so this exact file works
# whether you have one provider or several. See
# https://lmctl.com/lmctl/docs/manuals/teamfile-format for what a _MEMBER_
# line means and how to customize this after it's seeded.

_MEMBER_ alias=Lead     provider=${Provider1} model="${Model1}"
_MEMBER_ alias=Reviewer provider=${Provider2} model="${Model2}"
